==========================
echemdb-website Change Log
==========================

.. current developments

v0.2.1
====================

**Added:**

* Added 23 works to the best-practice reference table, among them stability and statistical benchmarking for water electrolysis, stability windows and data reporting for batteries and supercapacitors, IUPAC terminology for semiconductor electrochemistry and detection limits, and guidelines for electrochemical sensing.
* Added a News section to the website, built with the blog plugin of Material for MkDocs. The first post announces the news section and the acceptance of the echemdb data descriptor in *Scientific Data*. The first card on the home page links to the news.
* Added a link to the curated list of Python packages for electrochemistry (awsome-python-electrochemsitry) to the Software Tools page.
* Added the citation of the echemdb data descriptor, accepted for publication in *Scientific Data*, to the About page, the home page and a new Cite section of the CV Dataset page.
* Added an overview figure of the CVs for single crystal metal electrodes in aqueous electrolytes, arranged as in the periodic table, to the CV Dataset page. The figure is generated from the database during the build, so that it shows the numbers of the dataset version on the website. It always uses the complete database (also in fast builds) and is cached in ``generated/cache/`` between builds.
* Added a separate "Support" tab listing the institutions that fund and support echemdb.

**Changed:**

* Changed the tags of seven works in the best-practice reference table (Son 2023, Márquez 2024, Wang 2022, Wu 2021, Iglesias van Montfort 2023, Salvatore 2020, Nwabara 2020).
* Changed the citation of the echemdb data descriptor to the citation format of the website: authors, title in quotes and italics, journal, and **accepted** (or the volume in bold) followed by the year. The references to the *Data Science Journal* article on the About page follow the same format and link to its DOI. The Cite section of the About page lists the latest publication first and states which work to cite for which purpose.
* Changed the About page, which no longer contains the funding and support section. The homepage now links to the new Support page and also shows the logo of the National Institute of Chemistry, Ljubljana.

* Changed the funding and support logos on the homepage, which are now scaled so that they appear about equally large. The logo of the National Institute of Chemistry was cropped to remove its blank border.
* Changed the required version of unitpackage to 0.14.

**Removed:**

* Removed five works from the best-practice reference table that are not best-practice literature (Bloomquist 2024, Heenan 2022, Kibsgaard 2019, Pletcher 2018, Sebastián-Pascual 2020).

**Fixed:**

* Fixed the authors of the Journal of Power Sources good practice guide for battery papers (Li *et al.* 2020).
* Fixed the year of Grossfield *et al.* to 2019 and the key of Dutta *et al.* 2024 in the best-practice bibliography.
* Fixed the reference of Doblhoff-Dier *et al.* 2026, which now points to the published version in ACS Electrochemistry instead of the preprint.



v0.2.0
====================

**Added:**

* Added a "Notes and Limitations" and a "Contribute" section to the CV Dataset overview page.
* Added a note to the single component overview page that dissolved gases are only listed if stated in the original publication.
* Added a download section to each entry page, which provides the entry's Data Package (CSV and JSON) as a zip archive, together with a README and a LICENSE.

**Changed:**

* Changed the Contribute page to give an overview of contributions to the echemdb ecosystem, with a section per project linking to its contributing guide.
* Changed the Contribute section of the CV Dataset page to describe the ways to contribute data and link to the contributing guide of the electrochemistry-data repository.
* Changed the title of the CV overview page to "CV Dataset" and updated the description of the tags.
* Changed the curator's comment on entry pages to a warning admonition placed directly below the figure.
* Changed the electrochemistry-data version to 0.10.0.

**Removed:**

* Removed the step-by-step instructions for submitting source data and digitized data from the Contribute page, which are now part of the contributing guide of the electrochemistry-data repository.
* Removed support for Python 3.10, which reached its end of life in October 2026. The website now requires Python 3.11 or later.



v0.1.0
====================

**Added:**

* Added a release workflow with rever.
* Added a pull request template.

**Changed:**

* Changed the deployment to GitHub Pages to only happen when a new version is tagged.

**Fixed:**

* Fixed the Zenodo metadata, which was ignored since it was not named `.zenodo.json`, and its description, which did not describe the content of this repository.


